 logit
+
+Fit the model with:
+
+```bash
+prob4d identity calibrate \
+  outputs/calibration/identity-choices.json \
+  outputs/calibration/identity-labels.json \
+  outputs/calibration/identity-calibration.json \
+  --ridge 0.001 \
+  --probability-floor 0.000001
+```
+
+For choice set `s`, candidate `a`, standardized feature vector `x_sa`, and
+coefficient vector `beta`, the source probability is
+
+```text
+q(a | s) = softmax_a(x_sa^T beta).
+```
+
+Each declared calibration group receives equal total objective mass. Informative
+choice sets within one group then receive equal mass, so an object with more tracks
+cannot dominate solely through row count. Null-only sets remain in the artifact
+and deploy with exact probability one, but they do not dilute the fitted objective
+or inflate its proper-score and top-1 diagnostics. Every calibration group must
+contain at least one non-null choice set. Feature centring and scaling likewise
+give each informative choice set equal mass and each candidate equal mass within
+its set.
+
+The deployed probability floor is applied only after the conditional-logit fit:
+
+```text
+q_floor(a | s) = (1 - |s| epsilon) q(a | s) + epsilon.
+```
+
+The fit fails when `|s| epsilon >= 1`, rather than silently changing the candidate
+set or clipping it inconsistently.
+
+The content-addressed calibration records coefficients, feature normalization,
+regularization, probability floor, exact producer and association revisions,
+training collection and labels, calibration group IDs, equal-group log loss,
+multiclass Brier score, top-1 accuracy, and the explicit target-free claim
+boundary. These metrics are deterministic held-in optimization diagnostics; they
+are not a held-out calibration or promotion result. The frozen P2m gate must
+assess proper scores and downstream trajectories on disjoint groups.
+
+## Publishing portable mixtures
+
+Apply a frozen calibration to any compatible source-only choice collection:
+
+```bash
+prob4d identity build-mixtures \
+  outputs/target-free/identity-choices.json \
+  outputs/calibration/identity-calibration.json \
+  outputs/target-free/calibrated-mixtures
+
+prob4d identity validate-mixtures \
+  outputs/target-free/calibrated-mixtures
+```
+
+The destination must be new. It contains one standard
+`prob4d.material-identity-mixture` JSON file per target-local track and a compact
+manifest binding every choice-set ID, mixture ID, target endpoint, and calibration
+ID. Validation rejects missing or extra members, symlinks, path aliases, manifest
+tampering, mixture-ID drift, changed calibration lineage, and target-boundary drift. A null-only choice set produces probability one on the null candidate
+exactly.
+
+BayesianPhysTwin may then combine the source probabilities with a separately
+frozen prefix-only candidate likelihood and retain the existing exact null and
+physical-baseline fallback rules.
+
+## Frozen P2m experiment
+
+[`protocols/material-identity-p2m-v1.json`](../protocols/material-identity-p2m-v1.json)
+registers the first valid comparison:
+
+- `P0`: newest-window persistent reference;
+- `P2`: hard source-linked identity;
+- `P2m`: source-calibrated identity marginalization; and
+- `P3`: evaluation-only oracle identity.
+
+Association calibration, candidate-likelihood/power calibration, guard
+calibration, and downstream evaluation use disjoint object or simulation groups.
+Promotion requires a proper-score or physical-trajectory improvement over `P0`,
+bounded harmful accepted updates, no material worst-group regression, and exact
+fallback for every rejection. A negative result is retained without retuning the
+same target partition.
+
+## Claim boundary
+
+A valid calibration artifact establishes only reproducible source-side
+probabilities under the declared source labels and groups. It does not establish:
+
+- correct material identity on a held-out physical object;
+- calibrated physical-state uncertainty;
+- a safe or beneficial BayesianPhysTwin update;
+- improved Causal4D intervention prediction; or
+- state of the art.
